<%# Everything known about what this variation returns: the figure, whether it still
    describes the variation, what the last change did to it, and the runs that produced
    it.

    One partial because it is one broadcast. When a run finishes, the figure changes as
    well as the list of runs; replacing only the list would leave a stale number sitting
    beside a completed run saying otherwise. %>
<div id="return_to_player">
  <% missing = variation.missing_for_rtp %>
  <% figure = variation.latest_rtp_figure %>
  <% current = variation.rtp_figure_current? %>
  <% previous = variation.previous_rtp_figure %>
  <% game = variation.game %>

  <h2 class="font-mono text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-ink">Return to player</h2>

  <% if missing.any? %>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate">
      Not yet: <%= missing.to_sentence %>. A figure computed from a partial description
      would look like an answer without being one.
    </p>
  <% elsif figure.nil? %>
    <%# A run is already going: the page starts one when it finds nothing current. %>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate">
      Working it out. Evaluating an ordinary five reel game exactly takes tens of
      seconds, so it does not happen while you wait for the page.
    </p>
  <% else %>
    <% standing = figure.to_result.against(variation.target_rtp_min, variation.target_rtp_max) %>

    <p class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-4 gap-y-1">
      <span class="font-mono text-4xl <%= current ? "text-ink" : "text-slate" %>"><%= figure.to_percentage %></span>

      <% if !current %>
        <%# A figure for an earlier description is the last thing known, and showing it
            as though it described this one would present a wrong number as authority. %>
        <span class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-alert">out of date</span>
        <span class="font-mono text-xs text-slate">the description has changed since</span>
      <% elsif standing %>
        <span class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] <%= standing == :inside ? "text-signal" : "text-alert" %>">
          <%= { inside: "in band", below: "below band", above: "above band" }[standing] %>
        </span>
        <span class="font-mono text-xs text-slate">
          target <%= variation.target_rtp_min_percentage %>&ndash;<%= variation.target_rtp_max_percentage %>
        </span>
      <% else %>
        <span class="font-mono text-xs text-slate">no target set</span>
      <% end %>
    </p>

    <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-xs text-slate">
      <%# The method is shown because it will not always be the same one. %>
      <%= figure.exact? ? "Exact · computed from every outcome, not sampled" : "Sampled" %> &middot;
      <%= game.pays_by_ways? ? "#{number_with_delimiter game.ways_count} ways" : "#{game.paylines.size} paylines" %>
    </p>

    <%# Tuning is the activity of making a change and seeing what it did, so the figure
        before the last change is worth as much as the current one.

        Only while the figure is current. Beside an out of date figure this would read
        as the effect of the edit just made, which is precisely the thing not yet
        known. %>
    <% if current && previous %>
      <p class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-3 gap-y-1 border-l-2 border-rule pl-4 text-sm">
        <span class="text-slate">was <span class="font-mono text-ink"><%= previous.to_percentage %></span> before your last change</span>
        <%# Deliberately not coloured by direction. Lowering the return is often the
            intention, and the band above already says whether the figure is where it
            should be; tinting a fall red would call a change wrong for moving down. %>
        <span class="font-mono text-xs text-ink"><%= "%+.2f points" % figure.points_from(previous) %></span>
      </p>
    <% end %>

    <%= render "variations/rtp_history", history: variation.rtp_history %>
  <% end %>

  <%= render "variations/calculations", variation: variation %>
</div>
